{"name":"Alpine Race","hex":"#234162","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"alpine","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of, relating to, or inhabiting mountains, especially above the timberline.","Alternative letter-case form of Alpine: Of, relating to, or inhabiting the Alps, a large mountain range in Europe."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of several plants, native to mountain habitats, often grown in rock gardens."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/alpine"},{"term":"race","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A contest between people, animals, vehicles, etc. where the goal is to be the first to reach some objective.","Swift progress; rapid motion; an instance of moving or driving at high speed."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To take part in a race (in the sense of a contest).","To compete against in a race (contest)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/race"}],"entries":[{"title":"Alpine race","blocks":[{"text":"The Alpine race is an obsolete racial classification of humans based on a now-disproven theory of biological race. It was defined by some late 19th-century and early 20th-century anthropologists as one of the sub-races of the Caucasian race. The origin of the Alpine race was variously identified. Ripley argued that it migrated from Central Asia during the Neolithic Revolution, splitting the Nordic and Mediterranean populations. It was also identified as descending from the Celts residing in Central Europe in Neolithic times. The Alpine race was described as having moderate stature, neotenous features, and specific cranial measurements, such as a high cephalic index."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alpine_race","wikidata":"Q958572"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/Bundesarchiv_Bild_146-1987-121-09A%2C_Russland%2C_Hitler%2C_Mussolin%2C_von_Rundstedt.jpg/500px-Bundesarchiv_Bild_146-1987-121-09A%2C_Russland%2C_Hitler%2C_Mussolin%2C_von_Rundstedt.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/Bundesarchiv_Bild_146-1987-121-09A%2C_Russland%2C_Hitler%2C_Mussolin%2C_von_Rundstedt.jpg/500px-Bundesarchiv_Bild_146-1987-121-09A%2C_Russland%2C_Hitler%2C_Mussolin%2C_von_Rundstedt.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Rundstedt, Mussolini and Hitler, Russia 1941. Hitler identified Mussolini as part of the Alpine race.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABundesarchiv_Bild_146-1987-121-09A%2C_Russland%2C_Hitler%2C_Mussolin%2C_von_Rundstedt.jpg"}],"sounds":{"alpine":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/77/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-alpine.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/7/77/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-alpine.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-alpine.wav.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/7/77/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-alpine.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-alpine.wav.ogg"}],"race":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/46/En-us-race.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/4/46/En-us-race.ogg/En-us-race.ogg.mp3"}]},"pictures":[{"title":"003 Wild Alpine Ibex Sunset Creux du Van Mont Racine Photo by Giles Laurent","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/003_Wild_Alpine_Ibex_Sunset_Creux_du_Van_Mont_Racine_Photo_by_Giles_Laurent.jpg/500px-003_Wild_Alpine_Ibex_Sunset_Creux_du_Van_Mont_Racine_Photo_by_Giles_Laurent.jpg","ratio":0.6666666666666666,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:003_Wild_Alpine_Ibex_Sunse